  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-custom-profile",
      "text": "[中文说明](README.zh.md)\n\nYour own name and avatar, on the account row at the bottom left. Only what this machine shows changes. The account is not edited, and nothing is uploaded.\n\n> Package: `dsh-plugin-custom-profile` · Plugin id: `plugin-custom-profile`\n\nChange it at **Settings → Profile**."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "In the app: **Settings → Plugins → Install → Local directory**, and select this checkout. After the package is published, search for `dsh-plugin-custom-profile`.\n\nOr quit the app and run:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add /absolute/path/to/dsh-plugin-custom-profile\n```\n\nFor another profile, use `dsh plugin --profile <profile> add dsh-plugin-custom-profile`, or `github:<your-account>/dsh-plugin-custom-profile`. Nothing to build."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "To install by hand, symlink this directory into the profile's `node_modules` and append this to `cordis.patch.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n- insert:\n    - id: plugin-custom-profile\n      name: dsh-plugin-custom-profile\n```\n\nRestart if **Profile** does not appear."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "Set a name and an avatar, then **Save**. An empty name keeps the account name. **Reset**, then **Save**, puts the account name and avatar back. **Cancel** drops unsaved edits.\n\nPNG, JPG, WebP, GIF, or AVIF, up to 10 MB. Cropped to a square and stored as 128×128 WebP, or PNG if that fails. A GIF stays a single frame. Names are at most 32 characters."
    },
    {
      "section": "Also",
      "text": "- Signed out, the row is left alone. A collapsed sidebar gets the avatar only.\n- The custom row follows this device, not the account. Clearing site data or changing devices removes it.\n- Do not run another plugin that paints the same row. This one will not import that plugin's saved values.\n- Written against client `0.2.2-rc.1`. If the account-row markup changes, the plugin stops painting instead of breaking the page."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Node `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0`. `npm test` runs 57 tests. `lib/index.js` does nothing. `lib/client.js` is the browser bundle. A daily GitHub Action watches the [Harness page](https://www.deepseek.com/en/harness/). A newer client opens an issue for the `dsh-compat` agent."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
